    "updated_at": "2021-03-25T21:16:52Z",
    "body": "Hi @trajano, this is definitely something we should consider but might be overkill at the moment since our process is very simple. We just use [`cargo`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo) which is included as part of the rust toolchain. You can install it using https://rustup.rs/.\n\nOnce you have cargo installed you can use the following commands\n```bash \n# run the tests \ncargo test\n\n# build the debug binary (output to target/debug/starship) \ncargo build \n# build a release binary (output to target/release/starship) \ncargo build --release\n\n# build and run starship\ncargo run\n# you can also add extra arguments or flags here \ncargo run explain \n```",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
